# hello_world, ESP-IDF's example unchanged, with its PSRAM on: on top of the example's own
# configuration (firmware/build.sh names it). ESP-IDF's PSRAM driver then finds the PSRAM at
# start-up, tests it and adds it to the heap. Built for the chips with PSRAM in esp32sim whose
# validation images include it: the ESP32-S3 (sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3), the ESP32-P4 and the
# ESP32-S31, each on its devkit profile's PSRAM.
CONFIG_SPIRAM=y
